A data distribution describes how values are arranged or spread across a dataset.

Example

40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90

A distribution helps us understand:

Where values are concentrated.

How widely values are spread.

Whether the data is symmetric.

Whether extreme values exist.

Whether the data is skewed.



