20. Pareto Distribution

The Pareto distribution is a heavy-tailed distribution used to model situations where a relatively small number of observations may account for a large proportion of the total.

Example

A small percentage of customers may generate a large percentage of sales.

This idea is commonly associated with the 80/20 principle, although the exact percentages depend on the real data.

Key Point

Pareto → Heavy tail / unequal contribution


