22. QQ Plot

QQ stands for Quantile-Quantile.

A QQ plot compares the quantiles of sample data with the quantiles expected under a theoretical distribution.

It is commonly used to check whether data is reasonably consistent with a normal distribution.

Python

import scipy.stats as stats
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

stats.probplot(
    df["Marks"],
    dist="norm",
    plot=plt
)

plt.show()

Interpretation

If the points approximately follow a straight line:

> The data is reasonably consistent with the assumed normal distribution.



If there are large deviations:

> The data may not follow the assumed distribution well.




